-- ccc28-part24c-hearing-appeal.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), sections 757 to 761 (PART XXIV, Dangerous Offenders and Long-term Offenders): evidence of character,
-- the offender's presence at the hearing, appeals, disclosure to the Correctional Service of Canada, and review for parole. Layer 1 of part ccc28.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text,
-- and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- READING A RESULT: JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING where it is silent or limited by its own wording; the court's own judgments are inputs.
-- Section 756 is shown repealed ("[Repealed, 1997, c. 17, s. 5]") and has no function.

§ `Part XXIV, section 757: evidence of character`

-- "Without prejudice to the right of the offender to tender evidence as to their character and repute, if the court thinks fit, evidence of character and repute may
-- be admitted (a) on the question of whether the offender is or is not a dangerous offender or a long-term offender; and (b) in connection with a sentence to be imposed
-- or an order to be made under this Part."  A power ("may") under an "if" gate: NOTHING when the court does not think fit (fork F3). The "without prejudice" clause keeps the
-- offender's right to tender such evidence and does not itself say when the right exists: the section is silent on it.
DECLARE `s 757 purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 757(a) the question of whether the offender is or is not a dangerous offender or a long-term offender`
    `s 757(b) a sentence to be imposed or an order to be made under this Part`
    `s 757 another purpose`

-- src:16502 | 757 Without prejudice to the right of the offender to tender evidence as to their character and repute, if the court thinks fit, evidence of character and repute may be admitted
-- src:16503 | (a) on the question of whether the offender is or is not a dangerous offender or a long-term offender; and
-- src:16504 | (b) in connection with a sentence to be imposed or an order to be made under this Part.
@ref s 757 (src:16502-16504)
GIVEN `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `s 757 purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 757 evidence of character and repute may be admitted` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court thinks fit`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court thinks fit": a grant limited by an "if" gate; the section does not say that evidence of character and repute may not be admitted otherwise
    ELSE CONSIDER purpose
         WHEN `s 757(a) the question of whether the offender is or is not a dangerous offender or a long-term offender` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 757(b) a sentence to be imposed or an order to be made under this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 757 another purpose` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (a) and (b) are not closed with "only"

§ `Part XXIV, section 758: presence of the offender at the hearing`

-- (1) "The offender shall be present at the hearing of the application under this Part and if at the time the application is to be heard (a) he is confined in a prison,
-- the court may order, in writing, the person having the custody of the accused to bring him before the court; or (b) he is not confined in a prison, the court shall issue a
-- summons or a warrant to compel the accused to attend before the court and the provisions of Part XVI relating to summons and warrant are applicable with such modifications
-- as the circumstances require."
-- src:16506 | 758 (1) The offender shall be present at the hearing of the application under this Part and if at the time the application is to be heard
@ref s 758(1) (src:16506)
GIVEN `the application under this Part is to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has acted under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 758(1) the offender shall be present at the hearing of the application` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application under this Part is to be heard`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the hearing of the application under this Part": the duty is limited to that hearing, and the subsection is silent about any other
    ELSE IF `the court has acted under subsection (2)`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notwithstanding subsection (1), the court may"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16507 | (a) he is confined in a prison, the court may order, in writing, the person having the custody of the accused to bring him before the court; or
@ref s 758(1)(a) (src:16507)
GIVEN `the offender is confined in a prison at the time the application is to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 758(1)(a) the court may order the person having the custody of the accused to bring the offender before the court` MEANS
    IF `the offender is confined in a prison at the time the application is to be heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if at the time the application is to be heard (a) he is confined in a prison, the court may order": a grant limited by an "if" gate; the subsection does not say the court may not so order otherwise

-- src:16508 | (b) he is not confined in a prison, the court shall issue a summons or a warrant to compel the accused to attend before the court and the provisions of Part XVI relating to summons and warrant are applicable with such modifications as the circumstances require.
@ref s 758(1)(b) (src:16508)
GIVEN `the offender is confined in a prison at the time the application is to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 758(1)(b) the court shall issue a summons or a warrant to compel the accused to attend before the court` MEANS
    IF `the offender is confined in a prison at the time the application is to be heard`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if at the time the application is to be heard ... (b) he is not confined in a prison"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The custody order of paragraph (a) as a regulative rule: the court orders, in writing, the person having the custody of the accused (the keeper of a prison, in the core) to bring the offender
-- before the court. The text states no time for it.
DECLARE `s 758(1)(a) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 758(1)(a) order in writing the person having the custody of the accused to bring the offender before the court`

-- src:16507 | (a) he is confined in a prison, the court may order, in writing, the person having the custody of the accused to bring him before the court; or
@ref s 758(1)(a) (src:16507)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 758(1)(a) action`
`s 758(1)(a) the court's power to order the person having the custody to bring the offender` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MAY `s 758(1)(a) order in writing the person having the custody of the accused to bring the offender before the court`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (2) "Notwithstanding subsection (1), the court may (a) cause the offender to be removed and to be kept out of court, where he misconducts himself by interrupting the proceedings
-- so that to continue the proceedings in his presence would not be feasible; or (b) permit the offender to be out of court during the whole or any part of the hearing on such
-- conditions as the court considers proper."  (a) is a power with a "where" gate (JUST FALSE, listed in NOTES.md group (i)); (b) is a power with no gate beyond the hearing.
-- src:16510 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1), the court may
-- src:16511 | (a) cause the offender to be removed and to be kept out of court, where he misconducts himself by interrupting the proceedings so that to continue the proceedings in his presence would not be feasible; or
@ref s 758(2)(a) (src:16510-16511)
GIVEN `the offender misconducts himself by interrupting the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to continue the proceedings in the offender's presence would not be feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 758(2)(a) the court may cause the offender to be removed and kept out of court` MEANS
    IF `the offender misconducts himself by interrupting the proceedings` AND `to continue the proceedings in the offender's presence would not be feasible`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where he misconducts himself by interrupting the proceedings so that to continue the proceedings in his presence would not be feasible"

-- src:16512 | (b) permit the offender to be out of court during the whole or any part of the hearing on such conditions as the court considers proper.
@ref s 758(2)(b) (src:16512)
GIVEN `the application under this Part is being heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 758(2)(b) the court may permit the offender to be out of court` MEANS
    IF `the application under this Part is being heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- on such conditions as the court considers proper: the conditions are the court's, and the text does not state them
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during the whole or any part of the hearing": the power is limited to the hearing

§ `Part XXIV, section 759: appeals`

-- (1) "An offender who is found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender may appeal to the court of appeal from a decision made under this Part on any ground of law or fact
-- or mixed law and fact."  A power ("may"), with a named class of appellant, a named kind of decision, and named grounds: outside them, the text is silent.
DECLARE `s 759 ground of appeal` IS ONE OF
    `s 759 a ground of law`
    `s 759 a ground of fact`
    `s 759 a ground of mixed law and fact`
    `s 759 another ground`

-- src:16514 | 759 (1) An offender who is found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender may appeal to the court of appeal from a decision made under this Part on any ground of law or fact or mixed law and fact.
@ref s 759(1) (src:16514)
GIVEN `the offender is found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is from a decision made under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 759 ground of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 759(1) the offender may appeal to the court of appeal` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offender is found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender` AND `the appeal is from a decision made under this Part`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An offender who is found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender ... from a decision made under this Part": the right is given to a named class, and the subsection is silent about anyone else
    ELSE CONSIDER ground
         WHEN `s 759 a ground of law` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 759 a ground of fact` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 759 a ground of mixed law and fact` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 759 another ground` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "on any ground of law or fact or mixed law and fact" is not closed with "only"

-- (2) "The Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal from a decision made under this Part on any ground of law."  Limited by its own wording to a ground of law:
-- a ground of fact or of mixed law and fact is not covered (marginal reading (b)).
-- src:16517 | (2) The Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal from a decision made under this Part on any ground of law.
@ref s 759(2) (src:16517)
GIVEN `the appeal is from a decision made under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 759 ground of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 759(2) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal` MEANS
    IF NOT `the appeal is from a decision made under this Part`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "from a decision made under this Part"
    ELSE CONSIDER ground
         WHEN `s 759 a ground of law` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 759 a ground of fact` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on any ground of law": the subsection names the ground, and does not say that no other ground may be put
         WHEN `s 759 a ground of mixed law and fact` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on any ground of law": the subsection names the ground, and does not say that no other ground may be put
         WHEN `s 759 another ground` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on any ground of law"

-- (3) "The court of appeal may (a) allow the appeal and (i) find that an offender is or is not a dangerous offender or a long-term offender or impose a sentence that may be imposed or an
-- order that may be made by the trial court under this Part, or (ii) order a new hearing, with any directions that the court considers appropriate; or (b) dismiss the appeal."
DECLARE `s 759(3) disposition` IS ONE OF
    `s 759(3)(a)(i) allow the appeal and find that an offender is or is not a dangerous offender or a long-term offender or impose a sentence or make an order`
    `s 759(3)(a)(ii) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, with any directions that the court considers appropriate`
    `s 759(3)(b) dismiss the appeal`
    `s 759(3) a disposition the subsection does not name`

-- src:16519 | (3) The court of appeal may
-- src:16520 | (a) allow the appeal and
-- src:16521 | (i) find that an offender is or is not a dangerous offender or a long-term offender or impose a sentence that may be imposed or an order that may be made by the trial court under this Part, or
-- src:16522 | (ii) order a new hearing, with any directions that the court considers appropriate; or
-- src:16523 | (b) dismiss the appeal.
@ref s 759(3) (src:16519-16523)
GIVEN disposition IS A `s 759(3) disposition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 759(3) the court of appeal may make this disposition` MEANS
    CONSIDER disposition
    WHEN `s 759(3)(a)(i) allow the appeal and find that an offender is or is not a dangerous offender or a long-term offender or impose a sentence or make an order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 759(3)(a)(ii) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, with any directions that the court considers appropriate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 759(3)(b) dismiss the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 759(3) a disposition the subsection does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (a) and (b) are not closed with "only"

-- (4) "A decision of the court of appeal has the same force and effect as if it were a decision of the trial court."
-- src:16526 | (4) A decision of the court of appeal has the same force and effect as if it were a decision of the trial court.
