    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A decision of the court of appeal": the subsection speaks of that court's decision, and is silent about any other

-- (6) "Notwithstanding subsection 719(1), a sentence imposed on an offender by the court of appeal pursuant to this section shall be deemed to have commenced when the offender was sentenced
-- by the court by which he was convicted."  The day the sentence is deemed to have commenced is the day the trial court sentenced the offender.
-- src:16529 | (6) Notwithstanding subsection 719(1), a sentence imposed on an offender by the court of appeal pursuant to this section shall be deemed to have commenced when the offender was sentenced by the court by which he was convicted.
@ref s 759(6) (src:16529)
GIVEN `the sentence is imposed on the offender by the court of appeal pursuant to this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the offender was sentenced by the court by which he was convicted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 759(6) the day the sentence is deemed to have commenced` MEANS
    IF `the sentence is imposed on the offender by the court of appeal pursuant to this section`
    THEN JUST `the day the offender was sentenced by the court by which he was convicted`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a sentence imposed on an offender by the court of appeal pursuant to this section": the subsection is silent about any other sentence

-- (7) "The provisions of Part XXI with respect to procedure on appeals apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to appeals under this section."  The modifications are not
-- stated here; Part XXI is outside this range.
-- src:16531 | (7) The provisions of Part XXI with respect to procedure on appeals apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to appeals under this section.
@ref s 759(7) (src:16531)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 759(7) the provisions of Part XXI with respect to procedure on appeals apply to the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is an appeal under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- with such modifications as the circumstances require: the modifications are in Part XXI and in the circumstances, and the subsection does not state them
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to appeals under this section"

§ `Part XXIV, section 760: disclosure to the Correctional Service of Canada`

-- "Where a court finds an offender to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender, the court shall order that a copy of all reports and testimony given by psychiatrists, psychologists,
-- criminologists and other experts and any observations of the court with respect to the reasons for the finding, together with a transcript of the trial of the offender, be forwarded to the
-- Correctional Service of Canada for information."  The text states no time for the order.
-- src:16533 | 760 Where a court finds an offender to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender, the court shall order that a copy of all reports and testimony given by psychiatrists, psychologists, criminologists and other experts and any observations of the court with respect to the reasons for the finding, together with a transcript of the trial of the offender, be forwarded to the Correctional Service of Canada for information.
@ref s 760 (src:16533)
GIVEN `the court finds the offender to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 760 the court shall order that the reports, testimony, observations and transcript be forwarded to the Correctional Service of Canada` MEANS
    IF `the court finds the offender to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court finds an offender to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender"

DECLARE `s 760 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 760 order that a copy of the reports, testimony, observations and transcript be forwarded to the Correctional Service of Canada for information`

@ref s 760 (src:16533)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 760 action`
`s 760 the court's duty to order disclosure to the Correctional Service of Canada` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 760 order that a copy of the reports, testimony, observations and transcript be forwarded to the Correctional Service of Canada for information`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not order that the reports, testimony, observations and transcript be forwarded to the Correctional Service of Canada"

§ `Part XXIV, section 761: review for parole`

-- (1) "Subject to subsection (2), where a person is in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period, the Parole Board of Canada shall, as soon as possible after
-- the expiration of seven years from the day on which that person was taken into custody and not later than every two years after the previous review, review the condition, history and circumstances
-- of that person for the purpose of determining whether he or she should be granted parole under Part II of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act and, if so, on what conditions."
-- "As soon as possible" is open-textured and is not computed (fork F1). The dates the subsection does fix are computed: the day seven years after the person was taken into custody, and the day two years
-- after the previous review. A year is a calendar year (`add years` of daydate; fork F4).
-- src:16535 | 761 (1) Subject to subsection (2), where a person is in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period, the Parole Board of Canada shall, as soon as possible after the expiration of seven years from the day on which that person was taken into custody and not later than every two years after the previous review, review the condition, history and circumstances of that person for the purpose of determining whether he or she should be granted parole under Part II of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act and, if so, on what conditions.
@ref s 761(1) (src:16535)
GIVEN `the day the person was taken into custody` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 761(1) the day on which seven years from the day the person was taken into custody have expired` MEANS `add years` `the day the person was taken into custody` 7

GIVEN `the day of the previous review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 761(1) the last day for the next review` MEANS `add years` `the day of the previous review` 2

-- src:16535 | 761 (1) Subject to subsection (2), where a person is in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period, the Parole Board of Canada shall, as soon as possible after the expiration of seven years from the day on which that person was taken into custody and not later than every two years after the previous review, review the condition, history and circumstances of that person for the purpose of determining whether he or she should be granted parole under Part II of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act and, if so, on what conditions.
@ref s 761(1) (src:16535)
GIVEN `the person is in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sentence was imposed before October 15, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 761(1) the Parole Board of Canada shall review the condition, history and circumstances of the person` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a person is in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period"
    ELSE IF `the sentence was imposed before October 15, 1977`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (2)"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 761(1) (src:16535)
GIVEN `the day the person was taken into custody` IS A DATE
      `the day of the review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 761(1) the first review is after the expiration of seven years` MEANS
    IF Day `the day of the review` AT LEAST Day (`s 761(1) the day on which seven years from the day the person was taken into custody have expired` `the day the person was taken into custody`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection requires a review as soon as possible after seven years and says nothing of a review before then

@ref s 761(1) (src:16535)
GIVEN `the day of the previous review` IS A DATE
      `the day of the review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 761(1) the review is not later than two years after the previous review` MEANS
    IF Day `the day of the review` AT MOST Day (`s 761(1) the last day for the next review` `the day of the previous review`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than every two years after the previous review"

DECLARE `s 761 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 761 review the condition, history and circumstances of the person for the purpose of determining whether the person should be granted parole`

@ref s 761(1) (src:16535)
GIVEN `the day of the previous review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 761 action`
`s 761(1) the duty of the Parole Board of Canada to review the person again` MEANS
    PARTY `the Parole Board of Canada`
    MUST `s 761 review the condition, history and circumstances of the person for the purpose of determining whether the person should be granted parole`
    WITHIN (Day (`s 761(1) the last day for the next review` `the day of the previous review`)) MINUS (Day `the day of the previous review`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Parole Board of Canada` BECAUSE "the Parole Board of Canada did not review the person not later than two years after the previous review"

